  <model metaid="meta_chlorzoxazone_kidney" id="chlorzoxazone_kidney" name="Model for the renal excretion of 6-hydroxychlorzoxazone-O-glucuronide" substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <h1>Model for the renal excretion of 6-hydroxychlorzoxazone-O-glucuronide</h1>
        <p>Model for the renal excretion of 6-hydroxychlorzoxazone-O-glucuronide
encoded in <a href="http://sbml.org">SBML</a> format.</p>
        <p>Import and secretion are not modeled explicitly but a lumped excretion
reaction relative to the GFR is used to describe the urinary elimination
of the glucuronide.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>58-64 % of a 250 mg dose are recovered as 6-hydroxychlorzoxazone (free
and glucuronide) in the urine (Frye1998, Burckart1998, Vesell1995)</li>
          <li>71-74 % of a 750 mg dose (Desiraju1983, Kharasch1993)</li>
          <li>the renal clearance of total 6-hydroxychlorzoxazone is 464-506 ml/min
(Frye1998), above the GFR: a tubular secretion</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
